{"title":"Career Roadmap · Power Plant Engineer","role":"Power Plant Engineer","summary":"A Power Plant Engineer works on the operation, maintenance, performance, reliability and improvement of electrical power-generation facilities.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Power Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Power Plant Engineer works on the operation, maintenance, performance, reliability and improvement of electrical power-generation facilities."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines electrical engineering, thermal engineering, power systems, rotating machinery, instrumentation, control systems, plant operations and safety."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the type of plant, the engineer may work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Thermal power plants"},{"text":"Gas-based generation"},{"text":"Hydroelectric plants"},{"text":"Nuclear power plants"},{"text":"Solar power plants"},{"text":"Wind power plants"},{"text":"Combined-cycle plants"},{"text":"Battery/storage-integrated generation"},{"text":"Hybrid renewable plants"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a conventional power-plant pathway, the strongest foundation is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Thermodynamics","Electrical Machines","Power Systems","Turbomachinery","Boilers/Steam Systems","Instrumentation","Control","Plant Operations","Maintenance"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The modern Power Plant Engineer increasingly needs knowledge of automation, digital monitoring, predictive maintenance, renewable integration and energy optimization."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Career Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Power Generation","Electrical Systems","Thermal Systems","Turbomachinery","Instrumentation","Control","Maintenance","Plant Performance"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E. Power Engineering","Electrica